# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Successfully verified and validated the Vercel Web Analytics installation for this Next.js project. The analytics was already properly configured in the codebase, and I've ensured all dependencies are correctly installed.

## Current Implementation Status

### Package Installation ✅
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 (latest)
- **Status**: Already present in package.json and now fully installed
- **Location**: Listed in dependencies in web/package.json

### Configuration ✅
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.4.6 with App Router
- **Implementation Location**: `web/app/layout.tsx`
- **Import Statement**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- **Component Placement**: Added as `<Analytics />` at the end of the `<body>` tag in RootLayout

### Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly placed in the root layout following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects:

```typescript
// web/app/layout.tsx
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" dir="ltr" data-theme="light" className={`${inter.variable} ${arabic.variable} antialiased`} suppressHydrationWarning>
      <head>
        <script dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: boot }} />
      </head>
      <body className="min-h-screen">
        <div className="backdrop" aria-hidden><i /><i /><i /></div>
        {children}
        <Analytics />  {/* ← Correctly placed here */}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

